      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the fantasy theme. Let me focus on the task at hand.\n\nTo reset the sensor, you'll need to check the water level switch. The E15 error code is usually triggered by a faulty water level switch. You can try cleaning the switch by using a soft brush or a cloth to remove any debris or mineral buildup. If that doesn't work, you may need to replace the switch.\n\nAnother possible cause of the E15 error code is a faulty water inlet valve. If the valve is not closing properly, it can cause the water level switch to malfunction. In this case, you may need to replace the valve.\n\nTo access the water inlet valve, you'll need to remove the lower panel of the dishwasher. This will give you access to the valve and the water level switch. Be careful when working with the electrical components, and make sure to disconnect the power to the dishwasher before starting the repair.\n\nAs you work, keep in mind that the goblins of the kitchen are always lurking, waiting to strike. But in this case, it's just a pesky appliance that needs fixing.",
